 * increment, which is also the monolith's worst case (GAP-17), never a double one.
 *
 * Failure reporting (SI-10 / D-6): a permanent error (rejected parameters, e.g. a
 * string quantity) is logged and the element skipped, like utils/bestsellers.js:29-31
 * (catch -> return false -> only a console.warn downstream); a transient error (rate
 * limiting, transaction conflict, network) gets a bounded in-handler backoff and, if
 * it still fails, is reported through batchItemFailures so SQS redelivers it.
 */

const { DynamoDBClient } = require('@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb');
